    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "Yes there will be a small overhead via the DLpack conversion (no data copy on GPU, but some processing on CPU). You should be able to just pass a `torch.tensor` to any CuPy array creation routines like `cupy.array`. The CUDA Array Interface will be utilized for zero copy, but the overhead should be much smaller.\r\n\r\nFYI CuPy recently launched a Gitter channel: https://gitter.im/cupy/community. Feel free to ask questions there or on Stack Overflow (with a `cupy` tag)!",
